# Architecture

The backend follows Clean Architecture with 4 layers, each in its own project:

- **Domain**: entities, value objects, pure business rules. No dependencies on
  any other layer, no references to EF Core, ASP.NET, or AWS SDK.
- **Application**: use cases, repository/external service interfaces, input/output
  DTOs. Depends only on Domain.
- **Infrastructure**: concrete implementations (EF Core, Postgres, SQS, Secrets
  Manager, external integrations). Depends on Application (implements interfaces
  defined there).
- **Api**: controllers/endpoints, middleware, DI configuration, authentication.
  Depends on Application and Infrastructure only for composition (Program.cs).

## Dependency rules
- Domain never depends on anything.
- Application never depends on Infrastructure or Api.
- New business rules go into Domain or Application, never directly in the
  controller.

## Project-specific patterns
- API errors follow RFC 7807 Problem Details (don't return raw exceptions).
- Asynchronous processing (e.g., click tracking) always via queue (local or
  cloud SQS), never synchronously within the redirect request.
- All user input validated at the boundary (Application or Api), Domain assumes
  already validated data.
